<title>USA: Farmers &amp; Mechanics Q3 net profit.</title>
<headline>Farmers &amp; Mechanics Q3 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>MIDDLETOWN, Conn. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>			  Three months	  Nine months</p>
<p>		   1996     1995		 1996    1995</p>
<p> Interest inc  $9,847  $9,163	    $29,155  $27,225</p>
<p> Interest exp   5,199   4,656	     14,994   13,260</p>
<p>Net interest income</p>
<p>		    4,648   4,507	     14,161   13,965</p>
<p>Total loan provisions</p>
<p>		     262    2,525		  858    3,738</p>
<p>Net income (loss) before</p>
<p>  income taxes  1,133  (4,495)	     3,523   (3,467)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>		    1,120  (2,295)	     3,500   (1,267)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>  per share	0.67  (1.38)		 2.11  (0.76)</p>
<p> Avg shrs	 1,662   1,656		1,661     1,655</p>
<p>Full company name is Farmers &amp; Mechanics Bank NOTE: The bank said 3Q and first nine months 1995 included significant one-time asset charges for non-performing loan disposition and foreclosured properties and severance costs. It was not immediately available to quantify these charges.</p>
</text>
